  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 1280,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Does Pressure Keep The Deep Ocean From Freezing?\nNo. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 4160,
    "dDurationMs": 3640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But you were probably hoping for a more in-depth \nanswer, so let's take a deep dive to the bottom of  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 7800,
    "dDurationMs": 4680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the Mariana trench, the deepest part of the ocean.\nDown here, there's 11km of water pressing down on  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 12480,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you from above, and the weight of all that water \ngenerates around 1000 times atmospheric pressure. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 16680,
    "dDurationMs": 3640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And pressure can melt ice - like, you \nonly need 500 times atmospheric pressure  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 20320,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to melt ice down to negative four degrees \ncelsius. If you have 1000 times atmospheric  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 24000,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "pressure (like at the bottom of the Mariana \ntrench), then you'll melt ice down to around  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 27440,
    "dDurationMs": 4360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "negative nine celsius. But that's for fresh water.\nFor salty sea water, everything more or less gets  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 31800,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "shifted colder depending on the \nsalinity: on the ocean's surface,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 33640,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "salt water doesn't freeze until around two \ndegrees celsius below zero; at 500 times  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 37600,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "atmospheric pressure salt water doesn't freeze \nuntil around six degrees celsius below zero, and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 41360,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at the bottom of the Mariana trench, salt water \nwouldn't freeze until around 11 degrees below 0. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 45560,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But for various reasons related to circulation and \nsalinity and temperature and convection and the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 48840,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "fact salt water freezes into freshwater ice... \nfor complicated reasons, deep ocean water is  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 53280,
    "dDurationMs": 4280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "often around 0° to 4° celsius, and doesn't get \nmuch colder than 2 degrees celsius below zero,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 57560,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which are temperatures at which the \nwater would stay liquid from salt alone,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 60360,
    "dDurationMs": 3320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "even without the additional pressure. So while \npressure could in principle keep the ocean from  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 63680,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "freezing, it doesn't really get a chance.\nAlright, now's your chance to try out the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 69760,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "new math and science courses from this video's \nsponsor, Brilliant.org. This course shows you  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 74000,
    "dDurationMs": 3160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "how to analyze Airbnb data to figure out \nthe best place to buy a rental property,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 77160,
    "dDurationMs": 3560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and this one teaches you how to program by \ncoding a familiar-looking game. Hands-on  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 80720,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "problem solving like in these courses is a \nmethod proven to be more effective than just  "
    } ]
